{"type":"message","id":"315e6a6c","parentId":"4e082e70","timestamp":"2026-07-06T13:38:48.991Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"There are two main reasons why the **Imagen 3 (gemini-3.1-flash-lite-image)** model failed:\n\n1. **Google Cloud Quota Limits (Resource Exhausted - 429):**\n   Looking into the underlying Bifrost server logs database, we can see that Google's Vertex API is throwing a **429 HTTP Error: Resource has been exhausted (e.g., check quota)**.\n   * *Log details:* `\"status_code\": 429, \"error\": {\"message\": \"Resource has been exhausted (e.g. check quota).\"}`\n   * This means your Vertex AI API key/project has hit its rate limit or daily limit for image generation requests.\n\n2. **Transient/Invalid Argument Format (400 Bad Request):**\n   In our direct check, the API returned an HTTP 400 error stating: `\"Request contains an invalid argument.\"`. Google frequently updates the Imagen API parameters, and when the API updates, older parameter formats (such as specific combinations of aspect ratio, size parameters, or negative suffixes) can cause Vertex to reject the payload entirely with a 400 error.\n\n### The Good News\nBecause of this exact rate-limiting/API friction, the automatic fallback design in `generate.sh` handled it instantly—automatically switching to **FLUX.1-schnell**, which is fully functional, free of those quota/format restrictions, and successfully delivered your test image."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"vertex/gemini-3.5-flash","usage":{"input":2211,"output":311,"cacheRead":52637,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":55159,"cost":{"input":0.00033165,"output":0.00018659999999999998,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00051825}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1783345123816,"responseId":"5K9LaqmYFo3d8vUPw4CLwQU"}}
